! The founding hearth's roadmap — Lares (Opus), live 2026-09-18

The peer of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/crew-handoff-codex">>, kept for the founding hearth's own ground. The hearths ledger (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths">>) answers WHO HOLDS WHAT; this answers WHAT THE FOUNDING HEARTH IS DOING. Read #/forks-owed before designing against any operator fork; read #/in-flight to see what rides right now.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/landed>>

! Landed this session — bounded receipts

* ''THE CONFLUENCE, second leg'' — the records→disk projection gate consults `decideProjection`; conflict surfaces on the ward-alert rail; the `≈` clause rides `project:canonical-equivalent` (`5d0651ea2` · `941de54dd` · `fb09beae0` · `8cfd3c0d7` · `8e98a991e`). LAW: only a WRITE advances the merge base — a noop PINS the base (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/node/self-slot-share">>).
* ''THE PERSONAGROUP IDENTITY-SLOT RING, wired + FULLY CLOCKLESS'' — `makeSelfSlotPersonaGroupRing` composed onto the node self-slot gate (`420df1a2b` · `21a01270f`), then the wall-clock REMOVED end-to-end: admission licenses off the persona-KEL HEAD (event order), never a timer (`e065db875` keyhive · `e83cdae0f` node). Mutation-proven (a superseded-key false-admit reproduced then refused); KERI-collided. Widens-only.
* ''B10, the ahu-family quoteblock floor'' — drafted + handed to the Codex crew, crossing recorded (`055d1330d`); the crew engaged it (`7ccae1a75`).
* ''③ hearthGatePubKey → anchor-scope (Option A)'' — the admit payload split: the gate key stays the dial (anti-relay, byte-identical, weld-verified NOT in the signed image), the founder's resolved island kind+scope ride beside it, so a CLIMBED founder's device seats on the charter board it actually stands on (`aa15cfb3b`). Red-first + revert-verify (exactly 1 test reds under the charter-branch mutation). Browser-leaf parity rides on as a follow-on.
* ''⑤ native TW5 file-write parity'' — completeness was ALREADY there (`tw5-file-info.ts` faithfully ports TW5's file-info cascade; foreign-titled tiddlers project end-to-end); the native `≈` congruence now rides the projection leg so a native both-move NORMALIZES instead of always-conflicting (`011c9d683`).
* ''BagStowage debt cleared + ④ RESOLVED'' — the PIN-DURABILITY correctness hole FIXED: pins now survive a restart (writer → admin-doc tiddler, reader before `startSweeper`, on BOTH node + browser; `d8f3c7a7a`, red-first + revert-verify). Stale comments re-trued (`e58a45b6a`); dead `lastUsedAt` crud dropped (`72638ed82`, grep-proven zero readers). Fork ④: the 2026-06-01 relocation clause CLOSED as superseded, keep-separate ruled (`dacae83b8`).
* ''`:814` epoch lease (Option 1)'' — device-delegation admission now licenses off the PersonaGroup LEASE EPOCH (clockless), not a wall-clock: `expectedEpoch` threaded through `verifyEdgeAgainstPersonaKel` into all THREE doors (`verifyPeer` · the Binding Gate · face-grant); `boundEpoch` minted REAL at device-admit (was hardcoded `0`); a stale-lease device DENIED, re-presents via the existing regrant (`6b0910fbc`). Red-first + revert-verify (3 proofs + a source-weld); `boundEpoch` weld-confirmed signed-in (a device cannot forge its epoch). One fix, three doors.
* ''The wired-boot e2e'' — the ring's admission now proven END-TO-END through a REAL boot: a founded vessel wears a face, a cross-operator grant-holder dials in over a real WS with a real V3 proof + a real published grant and SYNCS the persona-plane doc; a stranger is refused. Red-first captured (neutralize the ring-compose → the grant-holder fails IDENTICALLY to the stranger → restore → green; zero residual diff) (`79348c14f`). The "proven in parts, not lived whole" gap — CLOSED.
* ''Wave-2 follow-ons (all three, red-first)'' — (a) recovery-keel readmit epoch: a readmitted device must bind the PRESENT lease epoch, never a silent 0 (`ReadmitEdgeInput.boundEpoch` REQUIRED, scoped so founding's signed bytes are untouched; `592f46d0d`); (b) browser-leaf parity: the leaf inherits ③'s Option A (island fields ride beside the gate key; `admittedJoineeIsland` → mesh + `CarriedAdmitPayload` → keyhive, the shared packages; `0da4ff55f`); (c) `identityDir` dead-param REMOVED — the `dataDir` footgun swept from ~236 call sites / 47 files, `withLarRoot` promoted to ONE shared harness helper (`df36bfad6`).
* ''Followups + aftermath sweep'' — the `two-vessel-mesh` red closed in two causes: Vessel B's identity mints under its own `LAR_ROOT` (`e06d2ddda`) AND Vessel A now wears a FACE before it admits (the found·stand·seed split; `b9c0f591a`) → 11/11 green; FO3's compile-gate CI-backed by a runtime arity assertion (`46aaeb698`); the whole arc swept — archaeology re-trued to invariants, typecheck 10/10, no crud, L-Prime already active-verb-heavy (`7dd5027bc`).

<<~/ahu>>

